      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016 The Society of Thoracic Surgeons. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Aneurysms involving a right-sided descending thoracic aorta with an aberrant origin of the left subclavian artery are rare. We describe the successful surgical repair of this vascular anomaly by the combined use of a left carotid to subclavian artery bypass followed by endovascular stent graft placement to exclude the aortic aneurysm. We also review the literature associated with this particular anatomic presentation."
      },
